      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That scratchy throat and difficulty swallowing are classic signs of anaphylaxis, a life-threatening emergency that requires immediate medical attention, not just an antihistory. Taking a massive 100mg dose of Benadryl is dangerous because it can cause dangerous heart rhythm issues, severe drowsiness, and even respiratory depression, which could kill you if your airway is already compromised. You must go to the ER or call emergency services right now, because waiting for sleep or saving money on a bill when your throat is closing off is a gamble with your life.",
